=== SURVEY ===
Web source AIThinkingIndicator.tsx is the streaming-but-empty affordance shown while an AI SSE stream
is open and the first delta.text frame has not arrived (the AiOutputPanel pendingChild). It is the
ONLY AI component in web/src/components/ai/ that reads just `useTranslation` and NO `useAiStream`
(verified: grep of all 60 AI components — every other one streams; this one does not). It therefore
has NO fetch / error / empty / stale / offline data branch. The file exports TWO presentational
pieces:
  • AIThinkingIndicator({ label? }) — a pulsing HelixMark + a medium-weight cyan label
    (`text = label ?? t('helix.thinking','Helix is thinking')`) + three bouncing dots
    (animate-bounce, staggered −0.3/−0.15/0s), above three shimmering skeleton lines (animate-shimmer,
    widths w-full / w-11/12 / w-9/12, staggered 0/0.3/0.6s). role="status" aria-live="polite"; the
    dots, skeleton, and mark are aria-hidden. Reduce-motion-aware purely via `motion-safe:` (the dots
    stop bouncing and the lines drop shimmer; the static skeleton remains).
  • AIThinkingDots({ label }) — the compact in-button form: a required label + the three bouncing
    dots only (bg-current), for a button's streaming state where the full skeleton is too tall. No
    hooks at all.
HelixMark.tsx: a 24×24 stroked double-helix SVG (two quadratic strands crossing at centre + two
rungs at y=7/y=17), currentColor stroke, strokeWidth 1.75.
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (only). Shared components: HelixMark. Charts/maps: none.
i18n keys: helix.thinking ("Helix is thinking", runtime default); ai.common.thinking ("AI is
thinking", the JSDoc-documented override verb). Both are reproduced in the P1/S10 table.
Existing native: no AIThinking* symbols anywhere (grep clean) → this surface adds no collision.
Canonical pattern studied: shared-surfaces/AIChatbotIndicator (Adapter/Model/Projection/Views/
Previews/strings/Tests) + the AIThinkingIndicator parity already embedded in AiOutputPanel.Views.swift
(AiOutputPanelThinkingIndicator — the pulse/bounce/shimmer + reduce-motion approach), reused here.

=== REASONING ===
- The web component is purely presentational (the loading/"model is working" affordance itself). The
  faithful native reproduction is its genuine render branches: (1) the full skeleton indicator vs the
  compact dots (the two exports), (2) motion vs Reduce Motion, (3) the default label vs a caller
  override. The generic data-state axes in the prompt template (empty/error/stale/offline) DO NOT
  exist in this source — it performs no fetch — so reproducing them would FABRICATE state the web does
  not have (a No-silent-drift / No-parity-shortcut violation in the other direction). They are
  therefore documented as N/A, not drawn. The surface still never renders a blank box: it always shows
  at least the static skeleton.
- Architecture mirrors the canonical AIChatbotIndicator leaf, minus the gate/connectivity axis it does
  not need:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): AIThinkingResolve (web t(key,fallback) seam), AIThinkingIndicatorInput
    (web label? prop), AIThinkingIndicatorMeta (surfaceSlug + the two web label keys/fallbacks),
    AIThinkingAccessibility (status label = the single visible label, per role="status").
  • Projection (pure): AIThinkingResolved + AIThinkingProjection.resolve — the verbatim port of
    `label ?? t(...)`, with an added null-safety refinement (empty/whitespace override → default) so
    the status is never voiced blank.
  • Model: AIThinkingTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; @Observable
    AIThinkingIndicatorModel (resolves the label via the i18n facade, emits view.opened once on first
    appearance — the indicator always presents, there is no gate); AIThinkingStrings i18n facade.
  • Views: AIThinkingHelixMark + AIThinkingHelixMarkShape (verbatim port of the HelixMark 24×24 SVG
    geometry as a stroked SwiftUI Shape), AIThinkingBounceDots/AIThinkingBounceDot (staggered bounce,
    AnyShapeStyle so the full form is cyan + the compact form inherits .foreground = web bg-current),
    AIThinkingSkeletonLines (GeometryReader-measured full/11-12ths/9-12ths widths via the shared
    TSSkeleton, whose shimmer already respects Reduce Motion), AIThinkingFullContent,
    AIThinkingCompactContent, and a reduce-motion-safe pulse modifier.
  • AIThinkingIndicator.swift: the two public Views — AIThinkingIndicator (full, binds the model,
    onAppear→start) and AIThinkingDots (compact, pure, no telemetry — it is part of its host control).
  • Previews (3) + strings + Tests (19).
- Reduce Motion: every animation gates on the environment (the Helix pulse, the dot bounce) or the
  shared TSSkeleton (shimmer), reproducing the web `motion-safe:`. It is NOT force-set in a preview:
  `\.accessibilityReduceMotion` is a get-only EnvironmentValues key (a read-only KeyPath, not a
  WritableKeyPath), so `.environment(\.accessibilityReduceMotion, true)` does not compile on this SDK;
  the inert path is instead exercised by the view tests (AIThinkingHelixMark(animate:false),
  AIThinkingBounceDots(active:false)) and is toggled in the canvas via the accessibility overrides.
- Rejected: porting Tailwind classes literally (used P1/S9 tokens); inventing empty/error/stale/offline
  chrome (the source has no data dependency — would be drift); HTTP/data in the view (none exists);
  a bare `HelixMark` name (would collide with another surface's internal mark in the single module —
  prefixed AIThinkingHelixMark).

